       The second portion of a bounce template consists of  message  text.  As
       the above example shows, template message text may contain main.cf $pa‐
       rameters.  Besides the parameters that are defined in main.cf, the fol‐
       lowing parameters are treated specially depending on the suffix that is
       appended to their name.

       ddeellaayy__wwaarrnniinngg__ttiimmee___s_u_f_f_i_x
              Expands into the value of the ddeellaayy__wwaarrnniinngg__ttiimmee parameter,  ex‐
              pressed  in  the  time unit specified by _s_u_f_f_i_x, which is one of
              sseeccoonnddss, mmiinnuutteess, hhoouurrss,, ddaayyss, or wweeeekkss.

       mmaaxxiimmaall__qquueeuuee__lliiffeettiimmee___s_u_f_f_i_x
              Expands into the value of the mmaaxxiimmaall__qquueeuuee__lliiffeettiimmee  parameter,
              expressed in the time unit specified by _s_u_f_f_i_x.  See above under
              ddeellaayy__wwaarrnniinngg__ttiimmee for possible _s_u_f_f_i_x values.

       mmyyddoommaaiinn
              Expands  into  the  value of the mmyyddoommaaiinn parameter.  With "smt‐
              putf8_enable = yes", this replaces ACE labels (xn--mumble)  with
              their UTF-8 equivalent.

              This feature is available in Postfix 3.0.

       mmyyhhoossttnnaammee
              Expands  into the value of the mmyyhhoossttnnaammee parameter.  With "smt‐
              putf8_enable = yes", this replaces ACE labels (xn--mumble)  with
              their UTF-8 equivalent.

              This feature is available in Postfix 3.0.

       The  usage and specification of template message text is subject to the
       following restrictions:

       •      The template message text is not sent in  Postmaster  copies  of
              delivery status notifications.

       •      If  the  template  message  text  contains non-ASCII characters,
              Postfix requires that the CChhaarrsseett:: template header  is  updated.
              Specify  an  appropriate  superset  of  US-ASCII.  A superset is
              needed because Postfix appends ASCII text after the message tem‐
              plate when it sends a delivery status notification.

